                <pb facs="0554" n="460" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg460"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baker, chargé, to Mr. Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Managua, Nicaragua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-10-23"><hi rendition="#italic">October 23, 1896</hi></date>.
                        (Received Oct. 28.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 719.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Following up the subject-matter of my
                    dispatches numbered 714, 715, and 716, I transmit herewith the official decree
                    of the Government of Nicaragua, and translation of the same, concerning the
                    abolition of the office of foreign relations in this Republic. This decree,
                    although dated October 16, was published in the Government paper, the Diario
                    Oficial, this day, October 23. It is, I believe, in every way consistent with
                    the information conveyed to you in my previous dispatches.</p>
                <p>It will be observed that according to article 3 of the decree this legation must
                    carry on its relations with the Government of Nicaragua through the medium of
                    the newly created “office of interior relations,” but it must address the Diet
                    on all affairs within its jurisdiction.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John F. Baker</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad interim.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d362-a1.xml" xpointer="d362-a1"/>
            </div>
